== Chapter I

#block(inset: (x: 1em))[
  #set par(justify: false)
  #text(size: 0.9em)[#emph[The Foundation of the whole ensuing Discourse laid in] Rom 8:13. #emph[The words of the Apostle opened. The certain connection between true Mortification and Salvation. Mortification the work of Believers. The Spirit the principal efficient Cause of it. What meant by the \[Body\] in the words of the Apostle. What by the \[Deeds of the Body.\] Life in what sense promised to this Duty.]]
]

#smallcaps[That] what I have of #emph[Direction] to contribute to the #emph[carrying] on of the work of #emph[Mortification] in Believers, may receive #emph[order] and #emph[perspicuity,] I shall lay the #emph[foundation] of it in those words of the Apostle, Rom 8:13. #emph[If ye by the Spirit do mortify the deeds of the flesh, ye shall live]\; and reduce the whole to an #emph[Improvement] of the great #emph[Evangelical] Truth and #emph[Mystery] contained in them.

The Apostle having made a #emph[Recapitulation] of his Doctrine of #emph[Justification by Faith,] and the blessed Estate and #emph[Condition] of them who are made by #emph[Grace] partakers thereof, vv. 1, 2, 3 of this #emph[Chapter,] proceeds to #emph[improve] it, to the #emph[Holiness] and #emph[Consolation] of Believers.

Among his Arguments and Motives unto #emph[Holiness,] the Verse mentioned containeth #emph[one,] from the contrary Events and Effects of #emph[Holiness] and #emph[Sin. If ye live after the flesh, ye shall die.] What it is to #emph[live after the flesh,] and what it is to #emph[die,] that being not my present aim and business, I shall no otherwise explain, than as they will fall in with the sense of the latter words of the verse, as before proposed.

In the words peculiarly designed for the Foundation of the ensuing Discourse, there is

1\. A #emph[Duty] prescribed; #emph[Mortify the deeds of the body.]

2\. The Persons are denoted to #emph[whom] it is prescribed; #emph[Ye]\; if #emph[Ye Mortify.]

3\. There is in them a #emph[Promise] annexed to that #emph[Duty, Ye shall Live.]

4\. The #emph[Cause] or Means of the Performance of this Duty, the #emph[Spirit]\; If ye #emph[through the Spirit.]

5\. The #emph[Conditionality] of the whole #emph[Proposition,] wherein #emph[Duty, Means,] and #emph[Promise,] are contained, #emph[If ye, etc.]

The first thing occurring in the words, as they lie in the entire #emph[Proposition,] is the #emph[conditional] Note; εἰ δὲ, #emph[but if. Conditionals] in such Propositions may denote two things.

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[1\. The #emph[uncertainty] of the #emph[Event,] or thing #emph[promised] in respect of them to whom the #emph[duty] is prescribed. And this takes place where the #emph[condition] is absolutely #emph[necessary] unto the Issue, and depends not itself on any determinate Cause, known to him to #emph[whom] 'tis #emph[prescribed.] So we say, #emph[If we live we will do such a thing.] This cannot be the Intendment of the #emph[conditional] Expression in this place. Of the #emph[Persons] to whom these words are spoken, it is said v. 1 of the same #emph[Chapter, there is no condemnation to them.]]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. The Certainty of the #emph[coherence] and Connection that is between the things spoken of. As we say to a sick man, If you will take such a #emph[potion,] or use such a remedy, you will be well. The thing we solely intend to express, is the #emph[certainty] of the Connection that is between the #emph[potion] or remedy, and #emph[health.] And this is the use of it here. The certain Connection that is between the #emph[mortifying of the deeds] of the Body, and #emph[living,] is intimated in this conditional particle.]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[Now the #emph[connection] and #emph[coherence] of things being manifold, as of #emph[Cause] and #emph[Effect,] of #emph[Way] and #emph[Means,] and the #emph[End]\; this between #emph[Mortification] and #emph[Life,] is not of Cause and Effect properly and strictly, #emph[for Eternal Life is the gift of God through Jesus Christ,] Rom 6:23. But of #emph[Means] and #emph[End]: God hath appointed this #emph[Means,] for the attaining #emph[that End,] which he hath freely promised. #emph[Means] though necessary have a fair subordination to an #emph[End] of free Promise. A #emph[Gift,] and a procuring #emph[Cause] in him to whom it is given, are inconsistent. The intendment then of this Proposition as #emph[conditional,] is, #emph[That there is a certain infallible connection and coherence between true Mortification and Eternal Life:] if you use this #emph[Means,] you shall obtain that End: If you do #emph[mortify,] you shall #emph[live.] And herein lies the main #emph[motive] unto, and #emph[Enforcement] of the Duty prescribed.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. The next thing we meet withal in the words, is the #emph[persons] to whom this Duty is #emph[prescribed]\; and that is expressed in the word #emph[Ye,] in the Original included in the Verb θανατοῦτε, if #emph[ye mortify]: that is, #emph[ye Believers]\; ye to whom #emph[there is no Condemnation,] v. 1 ye that are not in the #emph[Flesh,] but in the #emph[Spirit;] v. 5 who are #emph[quickened by the Spirit of Christ,] vv. 10, 11, to #emph[you] is this Duty #emph[prescribed.] The pressing of this Duty #emph[immediately] on any other, is a notable Fruit of that Superstition and self-Righteousness that the world is full of; the great work and design of #emph[devout] men, ignorant of the Gospel, Rom 10:3, 4. John 15:5. Now this #emph[description] of the #emph[Persons,] in conjunction with the #emph[prescription] of the #emph[duty,] is the main Foundation of the ensuing Discourse, as it lies in this #emph[Thesis] or Proposition.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[#emph[The choicest Believers, who are assuredly freed from the condemning power of sin, ought yet to make it their business all their days, to mortify the indwelling power of sin.]]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[3\. The principal #emph[efficient Cause] of the performance of this Duty, is the #emph[Spirit:] εἰ δὲ πνεύματι, #emph[if by the Spirit.] The #emph[Spirit] here, is the #emph[Spirit] mentioned v. 11 the #emph[Spirit of Christ,] the #emph[Spirit] of God, that #emph[dwells] in us, v. 9 that #emph[quickens] us, v. 11 the Holy Ghost, v. 14 the #emph[Spirit of Adoption,] v. 15 the Spirit that maketh #emph[Intercession] for us, v. 26. All other ways of Mortification are vain, all #emph[helps] leave us #emph[helpless,] it must be done by the Spirit. Men, as the Apostle intimates, Rom 9:30, 31, 32 may attempt this work on other Principles, by Means and Advantages administered on other accounts, as they always have done, and do; but (saith he) this is the #emph[work] of the Spirit, by him alone is it to be #emph[wrought,] and by no other power is it to be #emph[brought] about. Mortification from a self-strength, carried on by ways of self-invention, unto the End of a self-Righteousness, is the Soul and substance of all false Religion in the world: And this is a second Principle of my ensuing Discourse.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[4\. The #emph[Duty] itself, #emph[mortify the deeds of the Body]\; is nextly to be remarked.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[Three things are here to be inquired into,]]

- 1\. What is meant by the #emph[Body.]
- 2\. What by the #emph[deeds of the Body.]
- 3\. What by #emph[Mortifying] of them.

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[1\. The #emph[Body] in the close of the verse, is the same with the #emph[Flesh] in the beginning. #emph[If ye live after the flesh, ye shall die,] but if ye #emph[Mortify the deeds of the body]\; that is, of the #emph[flesh.] It is that which the Apostle hath all along discoursed of, under the name of the #emph[flesh,] which is #emph[evident] from the #emph[prosecution] of the #emph[Antithesis] between the #emph[spirit] and the #emph[flesh,] before and after. The #emph[Body] then here is taken for that Corruption and Pravity of our Natures, whereof the Body in a great part is the Seat and Instrument: The very Members of the Body, being made servants unto Unrighteousness thereby, Rom 6:19. It is #emph[Indwelling Sin,] the #emph[corrupted] Flesh, or Lust that is intended. Many #emph[Reasons] might be #emph[given] of this #emph[metonymical] expression, that I shall not now insist on. The #emph[body] here is the same with παλαιὸς ἄνθρωπος, and σῶμα τῆς ἁμαρτίας, the #emph[Old man,] and the #emph[body] of Sin, Rom 6:6 or it may #emph[synecdochically] express the whole #emph[person] considered as corrupted, and the seat of #emph[Lusts,] and distempered Affections.]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. The #emph[deeds] of the Body, the word is πράξεις, which indeed denoteth the outward #emph[actions] chiefly. The works of the #emph[Flesh,] as they are called; τὰ ἔργα τῆς σαρκὸς, Gal 5:19 which are there said to be #emph[manifest:] and are enumerated. Now though the outward #emph[deeds] are here only expressed, yet the #emph[inward and next Causes] are chiefly intended, the #emph[Axe is to be laid to the root of the tree]: The Deeds of the Flesh are to be mortified in their Causes, from whence they spring: the Apostle calls them #emph[Deeds,] as that which every Lust #emph[tends] unto: Though it do but #emph[conceive,] and prove #emph[abortive,] it aims to bring #emph[forth a perfect Sin.]]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[Having both in the seventh and the beginning of this Chapter treated of #emph[Indwelling] Lust and Sin, as the Fountain and Principle of all sinful Actions, he here mentions its Destruction under the name of the Effects which it doth produce. πράξεις τοῦ σώματος, are as much as φρόνημα τῆς σαρκὸς, Rom 8:6 the #emph[wisdom of the Flesh,] by a #emph[metonymy] of the same #emph[nature] with the former; or as the παθήματα, and ἐπιθυμίαι, the #emph[passions] and #emph[lusts of the flesh,] Gal 5:24 whence the #emph[deeds] and #emph[fruits] of it do arise: and in this sense is the #emph[Body] used v. 10. #emph[The body is dead because of sin.]]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[3\. To Mortify; εἰ θανατοῦτε, if #emph[ye put to death]: a #emph[Metaphorical] Expression, taken from the putting of any living thing to death. To kill a Man or any other living thing, is to take away the #emph[principle] of all his #emph[strength, vigor] and #emph[power,] so that he cannot act, or exert, or put forth any proper Actings of his own; so it is in this Case. #emph[Indwelling] Sin is compared to a Person, a living Person, called the #emph[old] man, with his #emph[faculties,] and #emph[properties,] his #emph[wisdom, craft, subtlety, strength]\; this (says the Apostle) must be #emph[killed, put to death, Mortified]: that is, have its power, life, vigor and strength to produce its Effects taken away by the Spirit. It is indeed #emph[meritoriously] and by way of Example utterly #emph[mortified] and #emph[slain] by the Cross of Christ: and the Old man is thence said to be #emph[crucified with Christ,] Rom 6:6 and our #emph[selves to be dead with him,] v. 8 and #emph[really, initially] in Regeneration, Rom 6:3, 4, 5 when a Principle #emph[contrary] to it, and #emph[destructive] of it, Gal 5:17 is planted in our hearts: but the whole work is by degrees to be carried on towards Perfection all our days. Of this more in the Process of our Discourse.]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[The Intendment of the Apostle in this prescription of the Duty mentioned, is, that #emph[The Mortification of Indwelling Sin, remaining in our mortal bodies, that it may not have Life and Power to bring forth the Works or Deeds of the flesh, is the constant Duty of Believers.]]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[5\. The #emph[promise] unto this #emph[duty] is Life: #emph[ye shall live.] The #emph[Life promised,] is opposed to the #emph[Death threatened] in the #emph[clause] foregoing: #emph[If ye live after the flesh, ye shall die]\; which the same Apostle elsewhere expresseth; #emph[ye shall of the flesh reap corruption]: Gal 6:8 or destruction from God. Now perhaps the word may not only intend #emph[eternal Life,] but also the spiritual Life in Christ which here we have; not as to the #emph[Essence] and #emph[being] of it, which is already enjoyed by Believers, but as to the #emph[joy, comfort,] and #emph[vigor] of it: As the Apostle says in another case, #emph[Now I live if ye stand fast,] 1 Thess 3:8. Now my Life will do me good; I shall have #emph[joy] and #emph[comfort] with my life: ye shall live, lead a good, vigorous, comfortable, spiritual Life whilst you are here, and obtain Eternal Life hereafter.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[Supposing what was said before of the #emph[connection] between #emph[Mortification] and #emph[Eternal Life,] as of Means and End, I shall add only as a second Motive to the Duty prescribed, that]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[#emph[The vigor and power and comfort of our spiritual Life, depends on the Mortification of the deeds of the flesh.]]]
